  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2018-05-01.litz.sbd.schoepsMK21.flac24192** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 16 songs; 93 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls the recording fantastic-sounding but says the 192 kHz upload doubles file size without any audible improvement [5]\n- **billystrings2018-05-01.litz.sbd.akg414.flac16**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 16 songs; 93 min [2]\n- **billystrings2018-05-01.litz.schoepsMK41v.flac16**: source not stated; 16 songs; 93 min [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2018-05-01.litz.sbd.schoepsMK21.flac24192**: taped by Keith Litzenberger; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Soundboard+Schoeps MK21's>KCY 250/05i>Schoeps VST62iu>Sound Devices MixPre-6 (24/192) [1]. Also: Soundboard blended with two Schoeps MK21 mics at the board, recorded on a Sound Devices MixPre-6 at 24-bit/192 kHz; Mixed in Nuendo 4, fades in Sound Forge Pro 11, tracked with CDWAV, converted to FLAC with Trader's Little Helper, tagged in Foobar2000 [1]\n- **billystrings2018-05-01.litz.sbd.akg414.flac16**: taped by Keith Litzenberger; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Soundboard + AKG 414's>Sound Devices 788t [2]. Also: Soundboard plus two AKG C414 XLS mics placed on stage, omni, spaced twelve feet apart, recorded on a Sound Devices 788t at 24-bit/48 kHz; Mixed in Nuendo 4, then downconverted to 16-bit/44.1 kHz with iZotope tools, and encoded to FLAC [2]\n- **billystrings2018-05-01.litz.schoepsMK41v.flac16**: taped by Keith Litzenberger; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps MK41V's>KCY 250/5i>Schoeps VST62iu>Sound Devices 788t [3]. Also: Recorded with Schoeps MK41V mics just in front of the soundboard, through Schoeps preamp and converter into a Sound Devices 788t; Captured at 24-bit/48 kHz, then converted with iZotope to 16-bit/44.1 kHz and encoded to FLAC [3]",
